                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A hard one to judge only as a yes/no recommendation.\nTheres little game here - not runing out of fuel, food and people - wich serves as needed pressure for making choices. Too little game for what itself proposes (i was expecting character changes in traits for example) for its normal price tag.\n\nBut for what little 'game' it contains it makes up for it with story and writting.\nOne of the most creative space opera journeys ive seen- one with more science in science fiction then pretty much any similar ive played and does Sci-fi right: what you meet on your journeys are the kind of interesting outcomes that are theorically viable considering how weird physics, evolution, space travel, time dillatation at relativistic speeds and others can shape the most outlandish outcomes.\n\nMy first run went down hill too quickly, so much i was ready to criticize on the forums... but i sticked with it.\nIt turned out to be a long journey downhill of 'bad choices' and ever smaller crew...\n...and to my surprise...\n...i reached my mission goal.\nAs an AI helping my crew find a new home for mankind. In the most unexpected way. One i would hardly agree with as a human, much less a 21st century one. But one i can't really argue against.\nI will avoid spoilers. Suffice to say i went immediatly here to recomend the game.\n\n-Don't come expecting challenging gameplay but challenging story choices.\n-Around half of these (or more, depending on rng and crew) aren't even informed choices - wich ends up being very fitting for the whole theme and feeling as dealing with the unknow and surprises is a unavoidable part of such a journey.\n-Have less variety and quantity in tone and encounters then similars ive played BUT\n-Have more well tought, written and mindscrapping sci-fi then any of those; Also encounters aren't a single dialogue box with few choices if any of similars but small adventures; Chunks of a choose-your-adventure/game book.\n-Could have been more, leaves me wanting- wich is as positive as negative: few games makes me want more of them.\n\nLike story games and sci-fi? Then go for it.\nThe amount here falls a bit on the short spectrun. Seems worth its current price tag.\nId feel bad if i bought it with a deep discount.",
